            0.673
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are the samples that change the colour of the flower extract to a shade of red the same as those that changed the colour of blue litmus paper to red? (Group A, Table 2.2)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.677,
            0.744,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are the samples that change the colour of the flower extract to a shade of green the same as those that changed the colour of red litmus paper to blue? (Group B, Table 2.2)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.738,
            0.745,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are the samples that do not change the colour of the flower extract the same as those that did not change the colour of red and blue litmus papers? (Group C, Table 2.2)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.799,
            0.744,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From the above activity, we can "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "conclude",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that the red rose extract can also be used to test the nature of the substances; hence, it is another example of an acid-base indicator. We can conclude that the red rose extract seems to give red colour in an acidic solution and green colour in a basic solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
